1
00:01:19,359 --> 00:02:01,889
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

2
00:02:04,019 --> 00:02:07,699
NO ANIMALS WERE HARMED DURING THE
FILMING OF THIS PRODUCTION

3
00:02:08,699 --> 00:02:11,180
Osman, where is my son?

4
00:02:13,360 --> 00:02:29,990
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com

5
00:02:40,100 --> 00:02:41,100
My Savcı!

6
00:02:42,180 --> 00:02:43,100
Thanks to God.

7
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:34,560
Where is my son?

8
00:03:35,780 --> 00:03:36,760
Who is that?

9
00:04:34,840 --> 00:04:35,760
Möngke!

10
00:05:07,620 --> 00:05:08,360
My son!

11
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:09,520
Möngke!

12
00:05:16,240 --> 00:05:21,160
How dare you take my son here as if he
is a prisoner?

13
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:24,040
We took him here the way he deserved.

14
00:05:30,960 --> 00:05:32,640
Just like a rabid dog!

15
00:05:56,820 --> 00:05:59,460
You’ve been looking for the one who
betrayed you.

16
00:06:04,720 --> 00:06:05,980
Here he is.

17
00:06:08,020 --> 00:06:11,920
You can call this dog, either your son
or a traitor.

18
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:17,780
It’s up to, Geyhatu.

19
00:06:27,820 --> 00:06:33,860
Today is the day we become
victorious, sons of Romans!

20
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:36,960
The dice is rolled.

21
00:06:37,520 --> 00:06:40,460
Today, for our holy lands…

22
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:44,720
… for our children’s future…

23
00:06:45,900 --> 00:06:49,720
… and for our honor, we must fight!

24
00:06:51,100 --> 00:06:55,900
If we lose this war, kill me at once!

25
00:06:58,840 --> 00:07:00,460
Since it means…

26
00:07:01,680 --> 00:07:07,680
… because of my pride, I sent you to a war
that we couldn’t win in the first place!

27
00:07:09,140 --> 00:07:13,920
But today, I won’t be responsible for the
death of our Empire and my soldiers…

28
00:07:14,700 --> 00:07:17,220
… but the Turks!

29
00:07:18,720 --> 00:07:19,480
Today…

30
00:07:19,960 --> 00:07:21,420
… the dice has been rolled.

31
00:07:22,420 --> 00:07:25,500
The victory is ours!

32
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:43,800
The victory is ours!

33
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:26,860
Cerkutay told me that you kidnapped
my son.

34
00:10:27,520 --> 00:10:28,560
Cerkutay, huh?

35
00:10:29,020 --> 00:10:30,260
Yes, Cerkutay!

36
00:10:39,040 --> 00:10:41,320
And you believed that, Geyhatu?

37
00:10:43,660 --> 00:10:47,740
Are you trying to tell he lied to me?

38
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:05,220
You and your soldiers will enter the
secret path here.

39
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:07,740
And I will open the gate for you.

40
00:11:07,840 --> 00:11:09,900
While Kayıs are busy with Geyhatu...

41
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:13,780
... we will take our Kulacahisar back!

42
00:11:41,740 --> 00:11:42,540
Stop!

43
00:12:10,620 --> 00:12:16,440
Just like you ordered, Alp Guards will be
poisoned and won’t be able to fight.

44
00:12:53,800 --> 00:12:56,520
Look, something is happening to soldiers!

45
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:35,460
Helen!

46
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:45,360
Dear Helen, today is the day.

47
00:13:46,180 --> 00:13:48,640
Today is our day!

48
00:13:49,360 --> 00:13:51,720
Thanks to you, feudal landlord Nikola.

49
00:13:52,700 --> 00:13:56,360
For the revenge of Sofia!

50
00:13:57,500 --> 00:13:59,480
You know what to do, right Helen?

51
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:02,960
Don’t worry about that.

52
00:14:11,240 --> 00:14:12,900
If I had come across to them…

53
00:14:13,960 --> 00:14:16,840
… I’d have killed your son and your
soldiers.

54
00:14:19,840 --> 00:14:22,820
Your soldiers were dead when I
arrived at the Tent.

55
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:27,720
And this traitor son of yours
wasn’t there.

56
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:32,520
Do you know where he was?

57
00:14:35,320 --> 00:14:39,760
He was torturing me to find out how
I found the cave he was hiding.

58
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:12,660
What are they talking about, Möngke?

59
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:15,120
They are lying, father!

60
00:15:23,980 --> 00:15:26,240
We still have lots of things to tell you.

61
00:15:27,420 --> 00:15:30,140
Our minds are sharper than our
swords, Geyhatu.

62
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:33,060
Don’t you forget about this.

63
00:15:43,160 --> 00:15:44,700
I will listen to you.

64
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:51,520
You only have one last chance to survive.

65
00:15:57,320 --> 00:15:58,360
Geyhatu…

66
00:15:59,820 --> 00:16:04,220
… you will either listen to fables which
will bring your death…

67
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:08,720
… or, to the facts which will make you
survive.

68
00:16:09,460 --> 00:16:10,740
The choice is yours.

69
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:15,920
You must be Bamsı Bey.

70
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:17,540
Yes I am.

71
00:16:18,620 --> 00:16:23,100
Now, open your eyes and be fair…

72
00:16:23,680 --> 00:16:30,020
… so that my face won’t be the last face
you’ll see before you die.

73
00:16:40,960 --> 00:16:46,200
I will listen to all of them in the Tent.

74
00:16:48,360 --> 00:16:54,560
They will tell me what happened since
the beginning.

75
00:17:16,400 --> 00:17:17,420
Alps!

76
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:01,400
My Rab…

77
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:06,680
… oh my Rab, grant our Bey to us.

78
00:18:08,280 --> 00:18:12,060
Grant our Bey to us, my Rab!

79
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:22,380
Oh, the one who can give remedy and heal.

80
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:42,520
What happened to our soldiers?

81
00:18:43,760 --> 00:18:47,180
Be ready and close the gates at once!

82
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:32,260
For Byzantine!

83
00:19:33,400 --> 00:19:34,700
He is finally here!

84
00:19:35,040 --> 00:19:39,100
In the name of our mother, Mary, and
our Lord, Jesus.

85
00:19:51,900 --> 00:19:54,200
For Byzantine!

86
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:21,160
My son set a trap for me, huh...

87
00:21:26,980 --> 00:21:28,920
... in order to kill me.

88
00:21:29,300 --> 00:21:31,460
He was trying to pull you in Sögüt.

89
00:21:35,120 --> 00:21:39,280
They were going to kill you in Sögüt and
blame my brother, Osman.

90
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:47,460
They are trying to use the hatred you have
for Osman who killed commanders of yours.

91
00:21:47,760 --> 00:21:49,000
Can’t you understand?

92
00:21:49,320 --> 00:21:51,920
Who exactly, Dündar Bey?

93
00:21:53,240 --> 00:22:00,300
It seems like this deficient son of yours
didn’t plan everything by himself.

94
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:01,960
Enough!

95
00:22:02,060 --> 00:22:03,240
Shut up!

96
00:22:08,200 --> 00:22:09,380
Yalvak Arslan…

97
00:22:12,180 --> 00:22:13,980
… do you have something to tell?

98
00:22:18,700 --> 00:22:23,700
Ertuğrul Bey is like a father figure to
me and we are also from Kayı tribe.

99
00:22:24,380 --> 00:22:26,000
I can't blame Ertuğrul Bey...

100
00:22:26,980 --> 00:22:31,080
... just like I can't blame his sons.

101
00:23:02,920 --> 00:23:04,080
The victory is ours!

102
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:15,360
Byzantine is reanimating once again!

103
00:24:19,520 --> 00:24:21,800
How can you still listen to them, father?

104
00:24:22,020 --> 00:24:23,120
Shut up!

105
00:24:26,640 --> 00:24:27,500
Hush!

106
00:24:35,600 --> 00:24:37,320
I listened to both sides.

107
00:24:49,900 --> 00:24:52,540
On the one side of the scale…

108
00:24:52,580 --> 00:24:54,520
… there are the words of your son...

109
00:24:59,100 --> 00:25:03,860
… and on the other side, Kayıs’ words.

110
00:25:07,420 --> 00:25:09,560
If you were me…

111
00:25:11,660 --> 00:25:13,980
… what would you do, Bamsı Bey?

112
00:25:26,800 --> 00:25:30,160
I wouldn’t believe the both sides.

113
00:25:44,860 --> 00:25:48,940
Words are tend to hide away the
intentions.

114
00:25:49,440 --> 00:25:54,840
Just like night hides away many horrible
things.

115
00:25:56,940 --> 00:25:59,180
He who drowses the facts…

116
00:26:03,400 --> 00:26:07,880
… and moves with words, eventually hits
the wall of facts.

117
00:26:14,020 --> 00:26:19,600
Neither Savcı Bey nor Osman Bey and your
son…

118
00:26:23,900 --> 00:26:28,240
… are not innocent unless they bring
evidence.

119
00:26:40,940 --> 00:26:44,160
They say Kayıs are judicious…

120
00:26:46,380 --> 00:26:49,480
… and I believe they are right.

121
00:26:51,800 --> 00:26:55,080
Then, listen to me carefully, Geyhatu.

122
00:26:58,360 --> 00:27:01,980
On the one side of the Scale of Justice,
there is your life…

123
00:27:03,240 --> 00:27:08,060
… on the other side, your son’s life.

124
00:27:14,660 --> 00:27:22,040
Now, with this case, you have to prove
that Genghis Khan is your ancestor.

125
00:27:40,080 --> 00:27:42,160
Do you have proof for your words?

126
00:27:45,220 --> 00:27:46,840
I gave you my life, father!

127
00:27:47,580 --> 00:27:50,580
I fought, I got wounded, and I almost
died.

128
00:27:50,640 --> 00:27:52,000
What else do you want?

129
00:27:52,020 --> 00:27:52,820
Shut up!

130
00:28:10,100 --> 00:28:11,400
Cerkutay...

131
00:28:16,280 --> 00:28:18,660
..., while your son was torturing my
brother,...

132
00:28:22,580 --> 00:28:24,040
... blurt out their plan.

133
00:28:28,600 --> 00:28:29,600
Tell us!

134
00:28:33,420 --> 00:28:36,340
When I asked your son how he was going
to kill you…

135
00:28:36,860 --> 00:28:40,680
… he said Cerkutay is trying to pull
him in Sögüt and we sat a trap there.

136
00:28:40,780 --> 00:28:41,480
Lie!

137
00:28:42,460 --> 00:28:44,080
All they say are lies!

138
00:29:30,060 --> 00:29:32,380
What are we going to do with the
prisoners?

139
00:29:33,640 --> 00:29:38,420
They are going to pay the double amount
of gold they demanded for our soldiers...

140
00:29:39,980 --> 00:29:42,500
... if they want them back!

141
00:29:47,680 --> 00:29:51,880
I like making people pay, Flatyus.

142
00:30:14,940 --> 00:30:16,680
May God protect you, Nikola.

143
00:30:55,320 --> 00:30:57,380
Brave sons of Byzantine!

144
00:31:02,560 --> 00:31:07,400
Cowards die for a thousand time
before death comes for them…

145
00:31:10,280 --> 00:31:15,180
… but you were born for a thousand
time in this castle today!

146
00:31:16,240 --> 00:31:18,780
Your manhood is equal to thousands
of cowards’…

147
00:31:20,040 --> 00:31:22,340
… and you have more freedom than them.

148
00:31:24,300 --> 00:31:29,080
Today, in this castle, you became
heroes for a thousand time!

149
00:31:36,100 --> 00:31:38,680
The victory is ours!

150
00:31:42,000 --> 00:32:03,180
The victory is ours!

151
00:32:04,280 --> 00:32:05,800
All of them are lies!

152
00:32:06,740 --> 00:32:08,120
Bring me Cerkutay.

153
00:32:08,500 --> 00:32:12,000
My Alp caught him and they are coming.

154
00:32:13,020 --> 00:32:15,140
He told us everything like warbler.

155
00:32:16,080 --> 00:32:17,280
He will be here soon.

156
00:32:21,640 --> 00:32:23,480
You will hear your own ears.

157
00:32:25,720 --> 00:32:29,140
Your son said, “When the time
comes, I will kill Argun Khan.”

158
00:32:29,860 --> 00:32:33,080
After that, I understood they were
collaborating.

159
00:32:33,980 --> 00:32:38,500
He was going to blame Osman then wash his
blooded hands in our clear water.

160
00:32:39,480 --> 00:32:41,260
And in the end, replace you.

161
00:32:46,480 --> 00:32:48,200
You ruined everything!

162
00:32:48,220 --> 00:32:49,900
I’m going to kill both of you!

163
00:33:08,240 --> 00:33:09,380
Father.

164
00:33:09,460 --> 00:33:11,000
Father, please forgive me!

165
00:33:11,400 --> 00:33:13,280
Have mercy on me!

166
00:33:14,100 --> 00:33:16,480
I made a mistake, Father.

167
00:33:18,280 --> 00:33:20,080
Please forgive me!

168
00:33:21,280 --> 00:33:24,900
I’m begging you, please forgive
me, father!

169
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:29,380
I made a mistake, father, please
forgive me!

170
00:33:30,660 --> 00:33:31,760
I'm begging you!

171
00:33:35,840 --> 00:33:37,760
Have mercy on me, father!

172
00:35:18,880 --> 00:35:23,160
I knew Osman Bey wouldn’t come
back without Savcı Bey!

173
00:35:24,560 --> 00:35:29,080
How could Osman Bey come back without
his dear brother, my Ahmet?

174
00:35:30,880 --> 00:35:34,040
They’ll work together and
get us out of this mess!

175
00:35:43,080 --> 00:35:45,720
You were angry at me because of Osman Bey.

176
00:35:45,720 --> 00:35:48,290
You were going to rip my
tongue apart, Hazal Hatun.

177
00:35:48,960 --> 00:35:55,160
Hatuns! We need to come
together. Enough of this!

178
00:35:55,160 --> 00:35:57,640
Thank God our Beys
returned safe and sound.

179
00:35:58,400 --> 00:36:01,240
Now it’s time to overcome
this trouble. Don’t.

180
00:36:05,240 --> 00:36:15,600
Sorry, my daughter. Of course, if Osman
Bey came without Savcı Bey--

181
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:35,840
Möngke is traitor!

182
00:36:39,920 --> 00:36:43,240
He wanted to kill Geyhatu!

183
00:36:44,520 --> 00:36:46,800
Geyhatu killed him!

184
00:36:46,800 --> 00:36:51,920
By punishing him, he reclaimed his honour!

185
00:37:04,960 --> 00:37:06,960
Get him out of here!

186
00:37:28,320 --> 00:37:32,560
Osman Bey and Savcı Bey saved our Tent!

187
00:37:34,520 --> 00:37:38,120
2 valiant brothers on the same path!

188
00:37:40,720 --> 00:37:44,840
Their story will be
graven on the mountains!

189
00:38:18,960 --> 00:38:23,400
So, you didn’t catch Cerkutay.

190
00:38:25,240 --> 00:38:31,880
You used his sinister name as bait.

191
00:38:33,000 --> 00:38:35,480
I saw that Cerkutay was tricking you.

192
00:38:37,680 --> 00:38:40,320
It was obvious that he
had his name in this.

193
00:38:47,480 --> 00:38:50,520
You’re a smart man, Osman.

194
00:38:58,080 --> 00:39:04,000
After you find Cerkutay,
you will see who is with him.

195
00:39:05,240 --> 00:39:10,840
When that time comes, allow
me to have my revenge, Geyhatu.

196
00:39:14,440 --> 00:39:18,520
You’ll be the first to find out.

197
00:39:20,920 --> 00:39:24,760
You’re now free.

198
00:39:36,520 --> 00:39:40,200
Say hello to Ertuğrul Bey.

199
00:39:46,360 --> 00:39:56,240
His mighty sons will stay on
these lands like noble mountains.

200
00:39:59,840 --> 00:40:03,840
That what I see.

201
00:40:42,120 --> 00:40:44,360
Yavlak Arslan…

202
00:40:54,920 --> 00:41:05,160
If there’s any disobedience,
you’ll be the one who pays for it.

203
00:43:24,520 --> 00:43:27,160
Burn all of these.

204
00:43:28,400 --> 00:43:31,720
Nothing of Turk’s will be left.

205
00:43:40,080 --> 00:43:42,200
Dirty nomads.

206
00:43:45,280 --> 00:43:52,480
Look at this. What are you even
doing with castles and city life?

207
00:44:27,000 --> 00:44:28,520
Shepherd!

208
00:44:35,440 --> 00:44:38,080
What were you doing in Kulacahisar?

209
00:44:41,680 --> 00:44:44,320
I’ll set you free.

210
00:44:46,880 --> 00:44:48,680
Under one condition.

211
00:44:53,200 --> 00:44:54,840
Give me that!

212
00:44:56,640 --> 00:44:58,480
Here!

213
00:44:59,840 --> 00:45:03,480
You’ll tell everything you
see here to Osman.

214
00:45:03,480 --> 00:45:09,080
Whatever you see word
by word! Look at my eyes!

215
00:45:09,680 --> 00:45:13,400
Can you see how entertained I am? Can you?

216
00:45:13,400 --> 00:45:15,920
Good. Will you tell him?

217
00:45:16,960 --> 00:45:23,240
You will tell him! Right?
You. will. Tell. him.

218
00:45:23,520 --> 00:45:29,600
Good. Long story short,
you will tell Osman.

219
00:45:55,960 --> 00:45:58,240
Vulgar people.

220
00:45:59,880 --> 00:46:06,080
Look at this. Shepherds.

221
00:46:23,320 --> 00:46:26,560
Victory is ours.

222
00:46:37,480 --> 00:46:39,960
I’d die for you, brother.

223
00:46:39,960 --> 00:46:43,280
I never doubted your
intentions and I never will.

224
00:46:43,280 --> 00:46:48,440
You made it on time. You’ve shaken
the enemy with your tricks.

225
00:46:48,440 --> 00:46:53,320
We’re the sons of Ertuğrul Gazi,
brother. Doubt doesn’t suit us.

226
00:46:54,640 --> 00:46:55,720
My brother.

227
00:47:17,800 --> 00:47:19,400
Brother?

228
00:47:28,120 --> 00:47:29,960
You’re okay.

229
00:47:32,440 --> 00:47:36,600
Mashallah, my valiants!

230
00:47:37,200 --> 00:47:42,560
As long as you stand
side by side, who can stand in your way?

231
00:47:42,560 --> 00:47:46,560
Who can destroy your traditions
as long as you protect each other?

232
00:47:46,560 --> 00:47:48,560
Mashallah, my valiants!

233
00:47:54,840 --> 00:47:55,880
Brother!

234
00:48:05,960 --> 00:48:07,960
Our father’s condition is bad.

235
00:48:21,720 --> 00:48:24,680
Dündar!

236
00:48:46,360 --> 00:48:48,360
Father!

237
00:48:59,400 --> 00:49:02,160
Get our father up.

238
00:49:05,360 --> 00:49:06,960
Father!

239
00:49:16,200 --> 00:49:18,640
Osman, come.

240
00:49:20,960 --> 00:49:22,280
Easy!

241
00:49:27,080 --> 00:49:31,040
Father! Come on now, easy.

242
00:49:43,640 --> 00:49:45,000
Brother!

243
00:50:03,640 --> 00:50:05,400
Savcı.

244
00:50:09,880 --> 00:50:12,120
Father!

245
00:50:21,800 --> 00:50:25,200
- Savcı.
- Father!

246
00:50:32,880 --> 00:50:34,760
Savcı.

247
00:50:52,640 --> 00:50:54,680
Father!

248
00:51:01,560 --> 00:51:03,400
Osman.

249
00:51:04,520 --> 00:51:12,040
Where is Osman?

250
00:51:13,800 --> 00:51:17,440
Father? I’m here.

251
00:51:30,600 --> 00:51:37,240
I’m here, father. I’m with you.

252
00:52:03,960 --> 00:52:06,760
I’m with you, father.

253
00:52:12,600 --> 00:52:15,840
Father…

254
00:52:31,840 --> 00:52:34,480
Don’t make me fall from your grace.

255
00:52:37,360 --> 00:52:43,520
Don’t make me fall from your heart.
I’ll always be with you.

256
00:52:55,520 --> 00:52:58,280
I’m always with you.

257
00:53:28,760 --> 00:53:31,080
- Father!
- Father?

258
00:53:36,600 --> 00:53:39,520
- Father!
- Father?

259
00:53:41,760 --> 00:53:45,880
Savcı, let us deal with our father!

260
00:53:47,440 --> 00:53:48,960
Father!

261
00:53:48,960 --> 00:53:51,520
Osman! Come, brother!

262
00:53:51,520 --> 00:53:55,240
Father, brother!

263
00:53:55,240 --> 00:53:58,040
- Come on brother!
- Father!

264
00:54:13,280 --> 00:54:15,360
Drink it, father.

265
00:54:47,320 --> 00:54:55,360
Abdurrahman Gazi, make way.
I’m here to see how Ertuğrul Bey is doing.

266
00:54:57,080 --> 00:55:03,880
His sons and brides are with him.
No one else is needed.

267
00:55:04,920 --> 00:55:11,800
Yavlak Arslan isn’t anyone else.
Yavlak Arslan is the Bey of Beys!

268
00:55:20,520 --> 00:55:27,680
My Osman! Do you see what
Abdurrahman Gazi is doing?

269
00:55:27,680 --> 00:55:30,960
He doesn’t allow me to see Ertuğrul Bey!

270
00:55:30,960 --> 00:55:33,960
What are you doing near Ertuğrul Gazi?

271
00:55:36,960 --> 00:55:42,240
Osman! Osman, you’re forgetting
who you are talking to!

272
00:55:42,240 --> 00:55:43,520
What am I forgetting?

273
00:55:47,040 --> 00:55:51,040
We’ll see, Yavlak Arslan.

274
00:55:52,040 --> 00:55:54,040
I didn’t forget what you did with Kuzgun.

275
00:55:55,440 --> 00:55:57,480
I’ll not let this go.

276
00:55:57,480 --> 00:56:02,120
If you’re behind this,
I’ll cut your head off!

277
00:56:05,320 --> 00:56:07,280
What’s the matter, Arslan Bey?

278
00:56:08,560 --> 00:56:13,880
Savcı Bey! Teach some
manners to your brother.

279
00:56:14,680 --> 00:56:18,560
Teach him how to speak to Yavlak Arslan.

280
00:56:19,840 --> 00:56:22,320
How can you tell someone who
challenged Geyhatu…

281
00:56:22,320 --> 00:56:25,040
… not to challange Yavlak Arslan?

282
00:56:44,600 --> 00:56:46,920
Kulucahisar has fallen, my Bey.

283
00:56:48,840 --> 00:56:55,120
Nikola sent me to tell you. He wanted
me to tell you what he did to Turks.

284
00:57:02,560 --> 00:57:04,760
What are you saying?

285
00:57:13,760 --> 00:57:15,960
What are you saying?

286
00:57:17,520 --> 00:57:22,240
Son! Stop, relax!

287
00:57:22,240 --> 00:57:31,840
Bamsı Bey! Let me go!

288
00:57:31,840 --> 00:57:35,880
Let me go! I’ll rip his lungs apart!

289
00:57:35,960 --> 00:57:39,480
- You don’t know what you’re doing!
- Let me go!

290
00:57:44,200 --> 00:57:47,080
Relax, son!

291
00:58:47,960 --> 00:58:52,160
The messengers who will take my news
to the Emperor are already on their way.

292
00:58:52,160 --> 00:58:56,480
Everyone in Constantinople
will hear what I’ve done today.

293
00:58:59,440 --> 00:59:03,560
They’ll say, “Nikola came yesterday
and took the castle today!”.

294
00:59:05,520 --> 00:59:10,200
“I wonder what he’ll do if we
sent him new armies?”, they’ll say.

295
00:59:10,200 --> 00:59:19,360
After destroying Kayıs, where will he take
the banner of Byzantine.” they’ll say.

296
00:59:19,360 --> 00:59:20,920
Yes!

297
00:59:26,080 --> 00:59:30,840
That’s what they’ll say. My soldiers
will be on patrol everywhere.

298
00:59:31,640 --> 00:59:35,240
They’ll take care of every Turk they see.

299
00:59:35,800 --> 00:59:42,080
Until there are no Turks left in Anatolia…

300
00:59:51,680 --> 00:59:56,080
Do you think he'd send us
additional units, Vlatius?

301
01:00:00,520 --> 01:00:06,960
We’ll enter Söğüt with this unit.
Kill every Turk in there.

302
01:00:06,960 --> 01:00:11,840
Until there are no tents, no
goats, no shepherds left.

303
01:00:11,840 --> 01:00:16,360
What do you think, Vlatius? Am I right?

304
01:00:18,080 --> 01:00:20,840
Vlatius, isn’t that right?

305
01:00:22,880 --> 01:00:29,360
An eye for an eye, Lord Nikola.

306
01:00:36,400 --> 01:00:39,280
An eye for an eye, my dear friend.

307
01:00:48,920 --> 01:00:51,160
An eye for an eye.

308
01:00:56,520 --> 01:00:58,640
Let’s grind our swords!

309
01:00:58,640 --> 01:01:02,440
Let’s go to Kulacahisar
after morning prayers!

310
01:01:02,960 --> 01:01:08,040
Let’s conquer the castle we took with
our martyrs blood, for our martyrs’ souls!

311
01:01:08,040 --> 01:01:10,360
You’re right, my Osman!

312
01:01:10,360 --> 01:01:15,800
He’ll instead hear that
the castle is reconquered!

313
01:01:15,800 --> 01:01:18,160
We wouldn’t be embarrassed.

314
01:01:20,080 --> 01:01:24,560
Attacking a castle is different
from attacking Tents, Bamsı Bey.

315
01:01:37,920 --> 01:01:39,400
Savcı, my son!

316
01:01:44,480 --> 01:01:46,560
That’s what you think?

317
01:01:48,120 --> 01:01:53,720
Attacking a castle is different from
attacking Tents, you say.

318
01:01:54,600 --> 01:02:04,920
But, son, I know that castle well
since we took it with my Osman.

319
01:02:08,960 --> 01:02:11,200
But it’s different this time.

320
01:02:12,120 --> 01:02:15,510
There are prisoners in the castle. We
need to think about their lives.

321
01:02:16,360 --> 01:02:22,640
Savcı Bey is right. We need
to get our minds together.

322
01:02:24,440 --> 01:02:28,320
First thing in the morning, we should
get the Beys together to decide.

323
01:02:33,400 --> 01:02:36,440
It’s important. We need to consult them.

324
01:02:41,240 --> 01:02:44,680
I’ll be at the castle’s doors first
thing in the morning.

325
01:02:44,680 --> 01:02:47,280
- Osman.
- Brother!

326
01:02:49,480 --> 01:02:51,400
I am the Head Alp, Osman.

327
01:03:10,400 --> 01:03:13,520
Osman!

328
01:04:05,840 --> 01:04:10,120
They took the castle while we
were dealing with Geyhatu! Dogs!

329
01:04:10,120 --> 01:04:12,120
They knew!

330
01:04:13,800 --> 01:04:15,600
What will we do now, brother?

331
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:31,720
Alps!

332
01:04:35,560 --> 01:04:40,400
Am I mistaken or are you
talking about what to do?

333
01:04:50,840 --> 01:04:53,160
We’ll take our hostages back!

334
01:04:54,200 --> 01:04:57,760
Bring the golds we took
from that Greek infidel.

335
01:04:59,280 --> 01:05:03,640
My Bey. Will we give those
infidels gold like rewards?

336
01:05:03,640 --> 01:05:08,760
I’d give everything in
the world for a Turk’s life.

337
01:05:10,200 --> 01:05:11,920
Thank you, my Bey.

338
01:05:11,920 --> 01:05:15,080
Instead of standing here,
sharpen your swords!

339
01:05:15,080 --> 01:05:18,400
My Bey. What about Savcı Bey?

340
01:05:18,400 --> 01:05:20,920
We’ll take the castle
back tomorrow, I said.

341
01:05:22,280 --> 01:05:24,120
Thank you, my Bey.

342
01:05:25,760 --> 01:05:30,720
We can’t rest now.
We’ll take what is ours back.

343
01:05:30,720 --> 01:05:33,280
We will, with Allah’s permission!

344
01:05:33,280 --> 01:05:36,840
- We’ll fly our banner!
- With Allah’s permission!

345
01:05:36,840 --> 01:05:41,280
- We’ll conquer many more castles!
- Allahu Akbar!

346
01:05:41,280 --> 01:05:47,680
We’ll found our Beylic in these
lands my father conquered!

347
01:05:47,680 --> 01:05:49,960
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

348
01:05:49,960 --> 01:05:56,200
Brothers! Those who
believe are victorious!

349
01:05:58,720 --> 01:06:07,680
Those who sharpen their swords with faith, stand
side by side, walk together are victorious!

350
01:06:10,720 --> 01:06:19,840
Muslim Turks walking Muhammed Mustapha's
path, his highness, are victorious.

351
01:06:19,840 --> 01:06:23,960
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

352
01:06:23,960 --> 01:06:25,720
Now!

353
01:06:27,280 --> 01:06:28,760
Time to be victorious!

354
01:06:28,760 --> 01:06:33,440
- Allahu Akbar!
- Allahu Akbar!

355
01:06:38,920 --> 01:06:43,240
Savcı Bey. What if Osman does something
without our knowledge?

356
01:06:44,360 --> 01:06:48,480
Be at ease, Arslan Bey.
That won't happen.

357
01:06:50,400 --> 01:06:55,240
It won't happen you say. Like it
didn't happen before, Savcı Bey!

358
01:06:55,800 --> 01:07:01,000
I will happen again. This boy
will do as he knows again.

359
01:07:02,600 --> 01:07:10,360
Arslan Bey! The one you call a boy
is Osman, son of Ertuğrul Gazi!

360
01:07:11,560 --> 01:07:13,280
Choose your words carefully.

361
01:07:15,800 --> 01:07:21,800
Everyone is mad. No one is in
the mood to listen to these words.

362
01:07:22,640 --> 01:07:26,000
You are their elder.
You should be calm.

363
01:07:26,000 --> 01:07:31,800
You're right, Dündar Bey. But in this
Tent, there's no respect...

364
01:07:31,800 --> 01:07:34,000
... for elders or any titles.

365
01:07:34,640 --> 01:07:36,440
Nothing has order.

366
01:07:37,160 --> 01:07:46,120
Savcı Bey, you're the First Alp. How long
will you listen to Osman Bey?

367
01:07:46,520 --> 01:07:48,320
This matter is different, Arslan Bey.

368
01:07:48,320 --> 01:07:51,200
If he doesn't listen to me,
I'll break his bones!

369
01:07:51,760 --> 01:07:57,440
He will not act on his own,
if he does, he will pay for it!

370
01:09:31,479 --> 01:09:35,080
Seasons have passed since
the little one was born.

371
01:09:35,080 --> 01:09:37,600
Yet he couldn't drink his mother's milk.

372
01:09:41,720 --> 01:09:43,399
You're doing wrong.

373
01:09:45,319 --> 01:09:46,800
It is a sin.

374
01:09:52,479 --> 01:09:53,880
Aygül!

375
01:09:53,880 --> 01:09:56,400
What? Didn't you say you'd
look after him?

376
01:09:56,920 --> 01:10:00,880
Didn't you say you'd raise him
as long as she lives?

377
01:10:04,000 --> 01:10:06,880
You say Aygül but...

378
01:10:06,880 --> 01:10:08,440
I killed Aygül.

379
01:10:09,000 --> 01:10:13,880
I'll kill an unwanted kid too. Get it?

380
01:10:16,320 --> 01:10:18,840
You'll stick to our agreement.

381
01:10:36,622 --> 01:10:41,462
Don't forget who I am.

382
01:10:43,222 --> 01:10:47,032
Then remember who you are.

383
01:10:49,003 --> 01:10:52,133
Remember what you gave up to live.

384
01:10:53,970 --> 01:11:00,590
I'll keep my promise.
But you'll remember what I told you.

385
01:11:10,932 --> 01:11:14,142
You'll get your revenge from
those who did you harm.

386
01:11:16,271 --> 01:11:19,191
Not from those who are beside you.

387
01:11:21,036 --> 01:11:27,756
Don't make me feel remorse for this child!
You promised!

388
01:11:29,110 --> 01:11:34,780
Aygül. Everything aside.
He's your child.

389
01:11:36,331 --> 01:11:39,111
Even though his father is Alişar...

390
01:11:42,356 --> 01:11:44,646
He's not my child.

391
01:11:47,882 --> 01:11:50,142
Not my child.

392
01:13:07,996 --> 01:13:11,060
I wish I could find your trace
by searching...

393
01:13:11,528 --> 01:13:13,903
...put my face to your trace's dust.

394
01:13:15,608 --> 01:13:17,968
I wish Allah destine it so I can see
your face.

395
01:13:19,591 --> 01:13:23,695
O' Muhammed, I need you.

396
01:13:31,640 --> 01:13:34,001
I wish there was a holy campaign
so I could join.

397
01:13:34,854 --> 01:13:38,166
I wish I could go down in the sands
of the road to the Kaaba.

398
01:13:38,583 --> 01:13:41,816
I wish I could see your face in my dream.

399
01:13:42,846 --> 01:13:46,614
O' Muhammed, I need you.

400
01:13:56,695 --> 01:13:59,551
Ali, Hasan and Hüseyin together...

401
01:14:00,753 --> 01:14:03,775
...their love is in the heart...

402
01:14:04,284 --> 01:14:07,554
...tomorrow in the last judgment...

403
01:14:08,238 --> 01:14:12,152
O' Muhammed, I need you.

404
01:14:21,767 --> 01:14:24,020
He lost that friend somewhere...

405
01:14:25,149 --> 01:14:27,766
...the love is in the heart...

406
01:14:28,869 --> 01:14:32,013
...tomorrow in the last judgment...

407
01:14:33,200 --> 01:14:38,691
O' Muhammed, I need you.

408
01:14:46,389 --> 01:14:51,710
You are loved in every heart...

409
01:14:53,572 --> 01:14:56,312
...by crying in the foreign lands...

410
01:14:57,169 --> 01:15:01,358
I need you, O' Muhammed. I need you.

411
01:15:03,263 --> 01:15:07,193
I need you, O' Muhammed.

412
01:15:58,708 --> 01:16:02,417
Who are you? What are you doing
in these lands?

413
01:16:02,460 --> 01:16:10,555
This is Ertuğrul Bey's lands.
Who are you to question me?

414
01:16:13,910 --> 01:16:25,507
It is time now. Now, you will try what
I taught you, on them.

415
01:17:46,430 --> 01:17:48,687
-Salam Alaikum.
-Alaikum Salam.

416
01:17:57,257 --> 01:17:59,618
Where is my brother Osman?

417
01:18:09,420 --> 01:18:12,880
Don't any of you know?

418
01:18:15,662 --> 01:18:19,596
Don't worry, my nephew.
He must have a reason.

419
01:18:20,321 --> 01:18:23,750
Wherever he is, he will come.

420
01:18:24,839 --> 01:18:30,427
No, uncle. No. He won't come. He is riding
his horse to bring more trouble.

421
01:18:38,160 --> 01:18:40,669
Not at all, brother. Let's wait.

422
01:18:41,571 --> 01:18:48,772
If he went to Kulucahisar,
he will pay dearly. Very dearly.

423
01:18:57,587 --> 01:18:59,788
Turks are coming!

424
01:19:14,794 --> 01:19:19,469
Open the doors! Ertuğrul's son,
Osman is here.

425
01:19:21,861 --> 01:19:25,480
They came to retake the castle,
with three men!

426
01:19:26,646 --> 01:19:31,721
Keep laughing, sons of dogs.
You'll see it soon.

427
01:19:34,139 --> 01:19:36,981
An army of three men.

428
01:19:59,781 --> 01:20:07,371
With 99 names of Allah, who creates when
he wants, who fills our hearts with faith.

429
01:20:12,993 --> 01:20:18,622
My beys, in this meeting, I want to
talk about two issues.

430
01:20:20,973 --> 01:20:25,762
Firstly, there is the matter of security
of Muslims who are in the castle.

431
01:20:28,043 --> 01:20:32,712
Nikola might ask for gold in return
for them. Inshallah, he does that...

432
01:20:32,712 --> 01:20:37,212
...so, we can save our brother by
paying the gold.

433
01:20:43,447 --> 01:20:47,717
Maybe they already killed those
innocent people.

434
01:20:48,074 --> 01:20:53,712
May Allah forbid, brother.
But, this is a probability.

435
01:21:02,695 --> 01:21:08,860
My beys, what do you say? Shouldn't we
send an envoy to save our brothers?

436
01:21:09,086 --> 01:21:13,844
Even if we make an agreement,
it doesn't mean that he will keep it.

437
01:21:15,166 --> 01:21:19,079
My nephew is right, he isn't the man
of his word.

438
01:21:21,161 --> 01:21:28,842
Nikola is a devil. His horns should
be ripped.

439
01:21:32,408 --> 01:21:37,850
What do you say, my beys? If this council
takes the decision of war...

440
01:21:38,288 --> 01:21:43,929
...we should talk about how will we mobilize
our troops and which bey will attack which gate.

441
01:21:49,231 --> 01:21:55,311
My bey, instead of sitting here like this
by putting our faith in the...

442
01:21:56,119 --> 01:22:01,551
...agreement with the infidel, we should
talk about how we will beat the enemy.

443
01:22:05,994 --> 01:22:10,876
If we will save our brothers by paying
gold, I say, we should do it.

444
01:22:11,584 --> 01:22:13,982
When will we take the castle!

445
01:22:13,992 --> 01:22:21,162
When we are ready. Of course, if my absent
brother doesn't do anything unprepared.

446
01:23:07,726 --> 01:23:18,911
Aygül. You will stay here. Take him.
Aygül, take him, my girl. Come on.

447
01:23:20,040 --> 01:23:23,218
It's not the time to be stubborn.
Hold him.

448
01:23:23,577 --> 01:23:26,761
Take him to his grandfather.
He should look after his groom's son.

449
01:23:27,170 --> 01:23:33,768
I'll so he can die of a heart attack, right?
You have no one else left than your father.

450
01:23:34,295 --> 01:23:38,759
Come on, don't be stubborn. He'll learn
when the time comes. Hold him.

451
01:23:40,055 --> 01:23:55,825
Come, my girl. Come on.
Come on. Don't leave the tent.

452
01:24:12,696 --> 01:24:24,824
Bala. They say that Osman went to
the castle. Is it true? I'm talking to you, Bala.

453
01:24:28,273 --> 01:24:33,253
-Nobody knows where Osman goes.
-You seem like you know it?

454
01:24:33,697 --> 01:24:43,055
No. I don't know either. But whenever Osman
disappears like this, he returns with trouble.

455
01:24:44,096 --> 01:24:46,951
What does your mouth speak of again,
Hazal Hatun?

456
01:24:47,453 --> 01:24:50,599
You are getting mad very fast, Bala.

457
01:24:53,438 --> 01:24:58,733
I grew up in a bey's tent. I know what
I speak of.

458
01:24:59,671 --> 01:25:03,424
Then, your ears should be listening now.

459
01:25:03,424 --> 01:25:04,824
Mother Selcan.

460
01:25:06,910 --> 01:25:07,910
Bala.

461
01:25:17,978 --> 01:25:19,438
My pretty girl.

462
01:25:22,955 --> 01:25:29,566
I heard that you travel in the mountains.
Well, I can't say that it doesn't fit you.

463
01:25:31,616 --> 01:25:41,458
Yes, I don't have the time to speak with fancy
words but I should speak two words to stop you.

464
01:25:45,415 --> 01:25:51,102
We didn't grow up in a bey's tent. We got
tanned in the uplands in summer, we froze...

465
01:25:51,590 --> 01:25:55,287
...in the tent in winter. We fought in the war
times and eat afterward.

466
01:25:59,708 --> 01:26:13,330
Now, let's come to the point. In these tents,
as every warrior is under Ertuğrul Bey's protection...

467
01:26:13,735 --> 01:26:20,335
...every woman is under my protection,
remember that.

468
01:26:33,421 --> 01:26:35,986
Where are the beys of the tents?

469
01:26:36,298 --> 01:26:42,296
-The council meeting.
-Good then. I'll see Osman after the meeting.

470
01:27:04,174 --> 01:27:06,149
Ya Hayy!

471
01:27:43,472 --> 01:27:45,465
We met again, Osman.

472
01:27:48,350 --> 01:27:50,825
I'm happy for you, Vladius.

473
01:28:05,000 --> 01:28:08,447
You don't even realize that the time
for a bargain has ended.

474
01:28:11,173 --> 01:28:13,073
A bargain is a sunnah.

475
01:28:17,580 --> 01:28:23,596
You found out that you can't pass
with weapons. Good.

476
01:29:20,083 --> 01:29:21,528
Osman.

477
01:29:35,087 --> 01:29:37,121
So, you are Osman.

478
01:29:40,728 --> 01:29:45,339
-Sheep shepherd Osman.
-So you are the sheep, huh?

479
01:29:55,972 --> 01:30:01,416
When you are a shepherd, you see
everyone as a sheep.

480
01:30:02,129 --> 01:30:06,915
When you are a sheep, you see
everyone as a shepherd.

481
01:30:16,149 --> 01:30:22,704
Isn't the petty tents that you build on
my holy lands, enough?

482
01:30:22,771 --> 01:30:26,454
So it wasn't enough that you tried to
take a castle without considering yourself.

483
01:30:26,463 --> 01:30:30,805
-We took it.
-But you couldn't hold it, Osman.

484
01:30:40,275 --> 01:30:42,495
We like suffering.

485
01:30:45,218 --> 01:30:49,323
What are those? Is it to save your tents?

486
01:31:11,848 --> 01:31:13,674
To take my captives.

487
01:31:16,663 --> 01:31:19,863
Will you take them with the golds
you took from us.

488
01:31:24,755 --> 01:31:31,597
I took this castle with my weapons.
I didn't steal it like you.

489
01:31:33,726 --> 01:31:35,345
Let me see.

490
01:31:35,478 --> 01:31:38,484
Not you. Soldier.

491
01:31:42,225 --> 01:31:45,319
I like the precautions.

492
01:32:08,657 --> 01:32:18,858
No, I wasn't wrong. This is a roman gold.
This is universal.

493
01:32:19,538 --> 01:32:25,083
Even barbarians like you use this gold.

494
01:32:43,421 --> 01:32:46,108
I have nothing to do with golds, Osman.

495
01:32:48,318 --> 01:32:51,201
So there will be no barter.

496
01:32:57,093 --> 01:33:04,339
I will finish you, your alps, and
the rest of the Turks.

497
01:34:07,426 --> 01:34:10,407
Ertuğrul Ghazi's son, Osman!

498
01:34:16,614 --> 01:34:21,726
I neither give up on my weapons nor
on my brothers!

499
01:34:41,553 --> 01:34:43,741
Now, release the captives.

500
01:34:46,629 --> 01:34:52,013
Or else I will cut the throat of this dog.

501
01:34:54,509 --> 01:34:57,503
Don't, Nikola. Don't!

502
01:35:17,864 --> 01:35:26,194
Use your brain, Osman. Do you think you
can leave this castle such as this?

503
01:35:27,649 --> 01:35:33,977
I'll leave as a wolf leaves a heard of sheep.

504
01:35:45,082 --> 01:35:54,394
Now get the captives to the gate or
say farewell to Vladius.

505
01:36:02,310 --> 01:36:04,083
Don't get any closer, infidels.

506
01:36:06,988 --> 01:36:08,822
Step back, dogs!

507
01:36:11,451 --> 01:36:17,203
It's the promise of Ertuğrul Ghazi's son,
Osman! If we live alive, I'll release Vladius.

508
01:36:22,121 --> 01:36:23,901
Do as he says.

509
01:36:25,921 --> 01:36:29,216
No, Nikola. No! No!

510
01:36:32,539 --> 01:36:34,698
Release the captives.

511
01:36:34,914 --> 01:36:40,873
No, Nikola! No! No! No!

512
01:36:54,855 --> 01:36:58,889
Don't leave me alive, Osman. Don't.

513
01:37:01,442 --> 01:37:02,811
Come on.

514
01:37:12,945 --> 01:37:14,193
Soldier!

515
01:37:20,241 --> 01:37:27,488
A master archer should kill Osman,
without hurting Vladius. Get out!

516
01:37:33,959 --> 01:37:40,060
The shop owners were already dying,
my bey. After the conquest of Kulucahisar...

517
01:37:40,060 --> 01:37:43,854
...we gained a second market but we lost
it too now. I don't know what will happen now.

518
01:37:46,338 --> 01:37:52,956
Potter, if you take the floor, speak
with words that will help.

519
01:37:54,197 --> 01:37:58,415
Now is not the time to talk
about money.

520
01:38:02,017 --> 01:38:05,486
-May I enter?
-Come.

521
01:38:14,627 --> 01:38:16,711
It must be important, Baysungur.

522
01:38:17,510 --> 01:38:22,261
We got a word from our scouts.
Osman Bey and his alps...

523
01:38:22,434 --> 01:38:25,358
...are riding towards Kulucahisar.

524
01:38:41,798 --> 01:38:46,956
I knew he would do that. I knew it.
I knew that would happen.

525
01:38:46,956 --> 01:38:48,806
What should I do about this man now?

526
01:38:49,372 --> 01:38:55,050
He acts as you taught him earlier.
Uncle, brother...

527
01:38:55,853 --> 01:39:00,529
Now, isn't it my right to teach
him his place?

528
01:39:01,357 --> 01:39:03,657
Osman...

529
01:39:12,115 --> 01:39:16,905
If Osman went to Kulucahisar castle...

530
01:39:19,500 --> 01:39:23,964
...he must've gone there to see the
situation of the castle he conquered.

531
01:39:26,144 --> 01:39:30,566
While we sit here like this...

532
01:39:30,674 --> 01:39:36,059
...and listen to the problems with money,
if Osman enthused...

533
01:39:36,780 --> 01:39:40,980
...that is for Allah and religion.

534
01:39:52,268 --> 01:39:57,840
Now, who will teach the valiant
who goes to save the Turks...

535
01:39:58,542 --> 01:40:01,268
...from slavery, his place?

536
01:40:01,729 --> 01:40:03,625
You say who?

537
01:40:05,677 --> 01:40:09,589
Ertuğrul Ghazi's son, Savcı Bey will!

538
01:40:11,055 --> 01:40:16,315
He will teach it to his brother,
his own blood!

539
01:40:18,329 --> 01:40:22,363
None should dare to intervene.

540
01:40:59,400 --> 01:41:04,063
Osman Bey! Osman Bey!
You came to save us!

541
01:41:20,734 --> 01:41:22,588
Vladius.

542
01:41:31,860 --> 01:41:35,014
Osman Bey! He is saving us!

543
01:41:45,933 --> 01:41:48,271
Vladius.

544
01:41:56,793 --> 01:42:00,910
Alps!
Alps!

545
01:42:05,921 --> 01:42:11,477
If you make another move,
I will kill Vladius right here.

546
01:42:47,301 --> 01:42:50,137
Open the gate!

547
01:42:55,569 --> 01:42:57,731
Open the gate!

548
01:43:02,531 --> 01:43:04,753
Osman Bey!

549
01:43:06,547 --> 01:43:12,551
-Keep your promise, release Vladius.
-I'll do it when I'm done.

550
01:43:14,909 --> 01:43:18,248
Look at this sheep shepherd.

551
01:43:23,276 --> 01:43:26,197
Look at this sheep shepherd.

552
01:43:27,892 --> 01:43:30,363
Open the gates!
Archers!

553
01:43:32,749 --> 01:43:37,077
If they don't release Vladius,
shoot them all.

554
01:43:45,485 --> 01:43:49,751
Come on. Come on, brothers.
Come on.

555
01:44:01,176 --> 01:44:06,213
-Close the gate.
-Keep your promise, Release Vladius.

556
01:44:11,039 --> 01:44:13,043
Shut it.

557
01:44:29,371 --> 01:44:33,528
You bunglers!
You idiots!

558
01:44:35,865 --> 01:44:39,728
You are good for nothing!
You idiots!

559
01:44:53,721 --> 01:44:57,225
Welcome, Selcan Hatun.
Welcome.

560
01:44:57,654 --> 01:45:02,214
-Thank you, Bamsı Bey.
-Your mission was harder than any of ours.

561
01:45:02,640 --> 01:45:05,230
May Allah please you.

562
01:45:06,083 --> 01:45:09,093
It's just getting started.

563
01:45:10,217 --> 01:45:13,777
How is my Ertuğrul Bey?
Tell me about him.

564
01:45:14,451 --> 01:45:19,891
Selcen Hatun, we had better pray.

565
01:45:19,949 --> 01:45:23,899
You also know that we don't give up
on hope from Allah.

566
01:45:24,257 --> 01:45:26,747
Oh, Ertuğrul Bey...

567
01:45:27,670 --> 01:45:32,630
- My Osman went to the castle, right?
- Yes, yes.

568
01:45:32,830 --> 01:45:36,610
Now his brother wants to punish him.

569
01:45:37,684 --> 01:45:42,834
He should pull himself together!
What punishment is this?

570
01:45:43,077 --> 01:45:47,977
Don't worry.
It is not that easy.

571
01:45:47,997 --> 01:45:51,183
Now, I shall go and see what
decision they have made.

572
01:45:51,183 --> 01:45:55,473
- I will come too.
- Eyvallah(thank you) Selcen Hatun.

573
01:46:10,240 --> 01:46:12,100
O The Healer

574
01:46:13,378 --> 01:46:15,168
O The Healer.

575
01:46:20,082 --> 01:46:23,072
Vladius is here!
Open the doors!

576
01:46:46,573 --> 01:46:48,443
Are they gone?

577
01:46:53,705 --> 01:46:55,395
A Roman...

578
01:46:57,409 --> 01:46:59,159
after being in this situation...

579
01:47:01,522 --> 01:47:04,122
will do a certain thing, Nikola.

580
01:47:14,465 --> 01:47:17,125
Are you going to comit suicide?

581
01:47:25,955 --> 01:47:29,135
How do you want to die, Vladius?

582
01:47:30,993 --> 01:47:33,203
By your sword.

583
01:48:04,978 --> 01:48:10,458
Roma's noble son Vladius,
As a result of your mistake...

584
01:48:10,874 --> 01:48:13,754
are you ready to die?

585
01:48:14,027 --> 01:48:16,127
I am.

586
01:48:33,066 --> 01:48:38,136
I am Savcı Bey, who Ertuğrul Ghazi
chose to be Head Alp...

587
01:48:38,150 --> 01:48:44,090
in the tribe meeting, in front of
every Bey.

588
01:48:49,967 --> 01:48:54,817
Osman Bey disobeyed my order...

589
01:48:58,658 --> 01:49:01,688
and endangered the captives' lives.

590
01:49:02,992 --> 01:49:07,802
When he returns to the tribe,
he'll be arrested.

591
01:49:33,695 --> 01:49:35,215
Savcı...

592
01:49:36,784 --> 01:49:42,814
Haste makes wastei my brother.
Maybe Osman saves the captives and return.

593
01:49:44,095 --> 01:49:47,265
Will you arrest your brother then?

594
01:49:48,908 --> 01:49:54,379
Gündüz Bey, this is a issue of justice.
Not a family issue.

595
01:49:54,379 --> 01:49:58,769
Eyvallah, Savcı Bey, Eyvallah (Okay).

596
01:50:02,849 --> 01:50:09,962
But don't forget, Osman saved your life
by disobeying you.

597
01:50:09,962 --> 01:50:14,732
So, will he disobey me every time?

598
01:50:15,155 --> 01:50:18,495
Am I a Head Sheep or a Head Alp?

599
01:50:21,827 --> 01:50:25,717
Savcı Bey...
Savcı Bey.

600
01:50:26,984 --> 01:50:33,884
You shall not make a big decision when
our Ertuğrul Bey is in bed.

601
01:50:36,124 --> 01:50:41,414
Such decisions are not made with rank
but with nobleness!

602
01:50:44,790 --> 01:50:49,130
Being Head Alp doesn't mean you
can do this.

603
01:50:51,508 --> 01:50:55,922
I wish you had talked to Osman Bey
this way, Bamsı Bey.

604
01:50:55,922 --> 01:51:00,032
- Because he acts like a Kayı Bey.
- He actually does...

605
01:51:01,819 --> 01:51:06,889
Because with every move he makes
shows he deserves to be a Kayı Bey.

606
01:51:14,184 --> 01:51:18,964
Welcome, aunt, but as you can see,
I am new also.

607
01:51:19,488 --> 01:51:20,918
Selcan Hatun.

608
01:51:22,624 --> 01:51:24,724
Don't exacerbate.

609
01:51:25,342 --> 01:51:30,762
Now it is time to talk about how
we can get Kulucahisar back.

610
01:51:47,513 --> 01:51:50,623
Are you ready to lose the last hope
of Roma in Turk war...

611
01:51:50,834 --> 01:51:56,004
and leave me all alone?

612
01:51:58,912 --> 01:52:03,582
Are you ready to destroy Roma's
future for your pride?

613
01:52:06,568 --> 01:52:11,558
- This is what Romans do!
- This was what Romans did!

614
01:52:11,798 --> 01:52:19,178
Because even if they had died, they would
know Roma would stand tall!

615
01:52:19,178 --> 01:52:24,058
Romans survived thanks to this honour,
Nikola!

616
01:52:24,464 --> 01:52:31,414
If you are smart, you get stronger,
Vladius, if you are strong, you be proud.

617
01:52:31,749 --> 01:52:34,769
Roma will be stronger, Vladius.

618
01:52:36,784 --> 01:52:44,704
Roma will be stronger, and then we will
deserve to be proud!

619
01:52:44,904 --> 01:52:49,114
- I can't live like that, Nikola.
- You have to!

620
01:52:52,941 --> 01:53:00,181
You have to take it all just like I did
when Geyhatu insulted me!

621
01:53:14,945 --> 01:53:16,905
Vladius...

622
01:53:17,128 --> 01:53:18,998
Kill me.

623
01:53:34,628 --> 01:53:37,968
- Do you want to die?
- Kill me.

624
01:53:47,328 --> 01:53:51,068
Who is going to kill your father's
murderers?

625
01:53:51,073 --> 01:53:52,743
Who!?

626
01:53:52,862 --> 01:53:55,042
Who is going to take revenge for your father?

627
01:54:05,794 --> 01:54:09,664
Are you going to kill yourself while
your father's murderers are there?

628
01:54:35,894 --> 01:54:38,174
Why are you not talking?

629
01:54:39,606 --> 01:54:41,716
Why are you silent?

630
01:54:43,094 --> 01:54:44,734
Talk!

631
01:54:45,213 --> 01:54:47,313
Save your dignity!

632
01:54:59,182 --> 01:55:00,932
Be quiet.

633
01:55:02,593 --> 01:55:04,613
I am talking to my son.

634
01:55:05,778 --> 01:55:07,028
Talk!

635
01:55:07,858 --> 01:55:10,308
What are we going to do with
Yavlak Arslan?

636
01:55:12,667 --> 01:55:17,787
Can Yavlak restrain Ertuğrul's sons?

637
01:55:18,514 --> 01:55:23,299
If Geyhatu wants, I'll schackle them
and make them obey.

638
01:55:23,299 --> 01:55:24,989
Enough!

639
01:55:33,522 --> 01:55:35,872
I have listened so much lately.

640
01:55:41,941 --> 01:55:47,301
Ertuğrul's Beys and sons talked
all the time.

641
01:55:48,518 --> 01:55:50,318
I listened to them.

642
01:55:52,261 --> 01:55:54,811
Do you know why?

643
01:55:55,880 --> 01:56:00,950
Because you can't get to know a
silent man.

644
01:56:02,782 --> 01:56:07,262
They talked...
I listened.

645
01:56:07,935 --> 01:56:09,774
Geyhatu is wise.

646
01:56:09,774 --> 01:56:12,754
Geyhatu doesn't know anything.

647
01:56:13,618 --> 01:56:16,238
He wants to learn.

648
01:56:18,591 --> 01:56:21,561
Bring me news...

649
01:56:22,515 --> 01:56:25,095
from Osman and Bamsı.

650
01:56:25,806 --> 01:56:28,181
If you wish, I want to do more.

651
01:56:28,181 --> 01:56:30,671
Make Osman and Bamsı...

652
01:56:31,283 --> 01:56:33,863
obey.

653
01:56:35,172 --> 01:56:37,492
I don't care about the others.

654
01:56:38,828 --> 01:56:41,598
You need to authorise me for that.

655
01:57:06,183 --> 01:57:08,923
I authorised you...

656
01:57:11,860 --> 01:57:14,300
in all the tribes in the region.

657
01:57:17,219 --> 01:57:20,429
From now on, you are Bey of the Beys.

658
01:57:22,299 --> 01:57:24,829
You won't regret it.

659
01:57:25,972 --> 01:57:28,392
Make them obey.

660
01:57:30,189 --> 01:57:32,799
Don't worry, glorious Geyhatu.

661
01:57:33,402 --> 01:57:38,312
Geyhatu is not glorious, but he
wants to be.

662
01:57:40,997 --> 01:57:43,417
Mongke is not here now!

663
01:57:44,934 --> 01:57:47,344
Mongke is dead!

664
01:58:39,645 --> 01:58:41,875
My Osman Bey is coming!

665
01:58:41,945 --> 01:58:45,145
Osman Bey is coming!

666
01:59:23,380 --> 01:59:25,710
Thank you my Allah.

667
02:01:39,045 --> 02:01:41,005
Be ready, Alps.

668
02:02:21,421 --> 02:02:25,841
My Bey, are we still arresting him?

669
02:02:26,659 --> 02:02:28,699
My order is certain.

670
02:03:00,125 --> 02:03:02,555
Is your meeting done, brother?

671
02:03:03,905 --> 02:03:06,295
Have you talked it through?

672
02:03:07,040 --> 02:03:10,490
You disobeyed again, Osman Bey.

673
02:03:11,000 --> 02:03:13,700
You'll be arrested.

674
02:03:26,554 --> 02:03:28,934
How is going to do that, brother?

675
02:03:30,236 --> 02:03:33,619
Alps!
Arrerst him!

676
02:03:33,619 --> 02:03:35,159
Hay Allah!

677
02:03:40,229 --> 02:03:44,329
Don't you dare!
Don't you dare!

678
02:03:57,329 --> 02:04:00,489
I am talking to you Alps!

679
02:04:46,179 --> 02:04:47,686
Alps!

680
02:04:48,071 --> 02:04:49,771
Arrest him!

681
02:05:05,030 --> 02:05:07,420
Lower your swords.

682
02:05:07,596 --> 02:05:10,103
Lower your swords!

683
02:05:10,103 --> 02:05:11,884
Bamsı Bey.

684
02:05:11,884 --> 02:05:14,594
Don't mess things up.

685
02:05:14,607 --> 02:05:16,977
You are talking to the Head Alp!

686
02:05:23,722 --> 02:05:26,192
Head Alp Savcı Bey.

687
02:05:26,253 --> 02:05:29,043
Head Alp Savcı Bey!

688
02:05:31,831 --> 02:05:33,821
Hey people!

689
02:05:35,782 --> 02:05:38,152
Hey people!

690
02:05:39,031 --> 02:05:41,491
Look at here!

691
02:05:41,502 --> 02:05:45,272
If you want to see a Head Alp...

692
02:05:45,981 --> 02:05:48,531
Look at him.

693
02:05:50,664 --> 02:05:56,104
If you want to see a Kayı Bey...

694
02:05:57,843 --> 02:06:01,200
Look at him.

695
02:06:01,200 --> 02:06:02,680
Hey Mashallah(praise be)!

696
02:06:14,465 --> 02:06:19,155
He saved your captive brothers...

697
02:06:19,265 --> 02:06:24,325
while you are just talking and doing
nothing!

698
02:06:29,886 --> 02:06:34,182
Now who dares to touch him?

699
02:06:34,182 --> 02:06:35,712
I dare !

700
02:06:56,281 --> 02:06:58,611
- You, ha?
- Yes, I dare!

701
02:07:00,825 --> 02:07:02,235
Enough!

702
02:07:10,879 --> 02:07:13,689
Enough already!

703
02:07:17,333 --> 02:07:20,693
I am your big brother!

704
02:07:21,727 --> 02:07:26,577
Do you hear me?
I am your big brother!

705
02:07:28,184 --> 02:07:32,794
You neither listen to me, nor
consult to me.

706
02:07:33,800 --> 02:07:37,720
You just fight like cat and dog!

707
02:07:45,170 --> 02:07:49,990
Enough now, I won't see you like this
again. Osman!

708
02:07:51,128 --> 02:07:55,988
No one is going to disobey the Head Alp.

709
02:07:59,060 --> 02:08:06,050
Savcı! No one is going to arrest
their brother because of this.

710
02:08:09,567 --> 02:08:11,637
Brother!

711
02:08:12,458 --> 02:08:14,958
You are bossing me around.

712
02:08:15,503 --> 02:08:17,783
Hands off my brother.

713
02:08:40,732 --> 02:08:43,552
Savcı Bey!
Come!

714
02:08:45,351 --> 02:08:47,461
Our Bey is dying!

715
02:08:48,919 --> 02:08:50,959
Our father is dying!

716
02:09:04,653 --> 02:09:06,143
Father!

717
02:09:36,829 --> 02:09:41,499
Whatever happens, they are brothers
in the end of the day.

718
02:09:41,857 --> 02:09:46,807
They are sons of Ertuğrul Ghazi.

719
02:09:46,929 --> 02:10:10,759
Please contact us for any inquiries
turkision@gmail.com